{"allowed_english": [], "context": {"approved_glossary_entries": [], "input_freeze": {"hash": "sha256:38d35232207575a9b64e6d354e5c6f3f8cafce221a1dccb1f179ecb3f3476fcb", "path": "docs/evidence/categories-completion-p006-frozen.json"}, "locked_english_contexts": {"inventory:categories:04VB:paragraph/0004": {"context_hash": "sha256:788d1ea25188c47884a1189159ebb8aea52241666d451ef8ed06e11839310883", "inventory_id": "inventory:categories:04VB:paragraph/0004", "kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 151880, "byte_start": 151056, "file": "categories.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:a18160e2320acdea58e25b8188191014ba18c7d12100156a61318fe96c827bf6", "line_end": 4265, "line_start": 4248}, "owner_tag": "04VB", "parent_tag": "04VB", "semantic_path": "paragraph/0004", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04VB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y'$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$s : Y \\to Y'$", "MATH_0004": "$t : Y' \\to Y''$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$\\left(t \\circ s\\right)^{-1} \\left(t \\circ f\\right) = s^{-1} f$", "MATH_0007": "$f : X \\to Y'$", "MATH_0008": "$g : Y' \\to Z'$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0010": "$s : Z \\to Z'$", "MATH_0011": "$S$", "MATH_0012": "$s^{-1} \\left(g \\circ f\\right) = \\left(s^{-1} g\\right) \\circ\n\\left(\\text{id}_{Y'}^{-1} f\\right)$", "MATH_0013": "$f : X \\to Y'$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0015": "$s : Y \\to Y'$", "MATH_0016": "$S$", "MATH_0017": "$t : Z \\to Y$", "MATH_0018": "$S$", "MATH_0019": "$\\left(s \\circ t\\right)^{-1} f\n= \\left(t^{-1} \\text{id}_Y\\right)\n\\circ \\left(s^{-1} f\\right)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d4e5c7a1f9a7417d3a08371b0a166cf404f26d4339d08176f5504da398b1e7ff", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b821acf738035652abf48be3275243153018fa3f365f4e3d05c61d1667f46246", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nThis notation is suggestive, and the things it suggests are true:\nGiven any morphism <MATH_0001> in <MATH_0002> and any two\nmorphisms <MATH_0003> and <MATH_0004> in <MATH_0005>, we have\n<MATH_0006>.\nAlso, for any\n<MATH_0007> and <MATH_0008> in <MATH_0009> and all\n<MATH_0010> in <MATH_0011>, we have\n<MATH_0012>.\nFinally, for any <MATH_0013> in <MATH_0014>, all\n<MATH_0015> in <MATH_0016>, and <MATH_0017> in <MATH_0018>, we have\n<MATH_0019>.\nThis is all clear from the definition.\nWe can ``write any finite collection of morphisms with the same target\nas fractions with common denominator''.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:677575b083f31bfd1d35b2de90c8d7a280cdef6923713a6b1bc7877a5256e722", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:04VB:paragraph/0004"}, "state": "READY"}, "inventory:categories:0BM1:remark/0001": {"context_hash": "sha256:15b31f0d6a4dc6da286ffde8f3b779dc8d2543563c973367f62da863b3b2ad95", "inventory_id": "inventory:categories:0BM1:remark/0001", "kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 150614, "byte_start": 149275, "file": "categories.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:9d5dd911044cd2c57b8cb6332f96c76ebdb8a5b78aa7bf2a4915ee39a8628b23", "line_end": 4236, "line_start": 4213}, "owner_tag": "0BM1", "parent_tag": "04VB", "semantic_path": "remark/0001", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "04VB", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{remark-motivation-localization}", "MATH_0001": "$S^{-1} \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$S^{-1} \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$S^{-1} \\mathcal{C}$", "REF_0001": "\\cite[Section 10A]{Lam}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{remark}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{remark}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:15a1a0fa7cfb30eacb8d3e39ef1406b7c45cca6a1cfd45c5f8b44ddb48c4c27b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bf9d728e69ade54f59ca781dbe913956b12c54912bde43756781fc919a59319e", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nThe motivation for the construction of <MATH_0001> is to\n``force'' the morphisms in <MATH_0002> to be invertible by artificially\ncreating inverses to them (at the cost of some existing morphisms\npossibly becoming identified with each other). This is similar to\nthe localization of a commutative ring at a multiplicative subset,\nand more generally to the localization of a noncommutative ring\nat a right denominator set (see <REF_0001>). This is\nmore than just a similarity: The construction of\n<MATH_0003> (or, more precisely, its version for\nadditive categories <MATH_0004>) actually generalizes the\nlatter type of localization. Namely, a noncommutative ring can be\nviewed as a pre-additive category with a single object (the morphisms\nbeing the elements of the ring); a multiplicative subset of this\nring then becomes a set <MATH_0005> of morphisms satisfying LMS1 (aka\nRMS1). Then, the conditions RMS2 and RMS3 for this category and\nthis subset <MATH_0006> translate into the two conditions\n(``right permutable'' and ``right reversible'') of a right\ndenominator set (and similarly for LMS and left denominator sets),\nand <MATH_0007> (with a properly defined additive\nstructure) is the one-object category corresponding to the\nlocalization of the ring.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8198c38f1043980c5234cf0c50a801363bcd1add377991a726b08fe2d825f873", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:0BM1:remark/0001"}, "state": "READY"}}, "model_output": {"hash": "sha256:8183881d1da2d854ef34daa5b99758b2abcb01ad2ab83a0e27ba142e8cee221f", "path": "docs/evidence/categories-co